Question No: 78. Subsets

The Solution is in C++ Language.

Solution:

class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<int>> subsets(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<vector<int>> res;
        vector<int> subset;

        createSubset(nums, 0, res, subset);
        return res;        
    }

    void createSubset(vector<int>& nums, int index, vector<vector<int>>& res, vector<int>& subset) {
        if (index == nums.size()) {
            res.push_back(subset);
            return;
        }

        subset.push_back(nums[index]);
        createSubset(nums, index + 1, res, subset);

        subset.pop_back();
        createSubset(nums, index + 1, res, subset);
    }    
};

Approach:

The solution uses the Backtracking (Include/Exclude) approach to generate all possible subsets of the given array. 
For every element in nums, the algorithm has two choices: either include the element in the current subset or exclude it. 
First, the element is added using push_back() and the recursive function is called for the next index. 
After that, pop_back() is used to remove the element, which is called backtracking,
    and the function is again called for the next index without including that element. 
When the index reaches the size of the array, the current subset is complete and is added to the result. 
By exploring both choices for every element, the algorithm generates all possible 2ⁿ subsets.
